<!-- FAQ -->
<section class="faq" id="faq">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="heading">
      <div class="eyebrow">Frequently Asked Questions</div>
      <h2>Company Formation FAQs</h2>
      <p>Some common questions about establishing a business in the UAE.</p>
    </div>

    <details>
      <summary>What is the difference between Mainland and Free Zone?</summary>
      <p>
        Mainland and Free Zone companies operate under different
        licensing frameworks. Their permitted activities, operating
        rights and regulatory requirements depend on the applicable
        authority and business activity.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Can a foreign investor own 100% of a UAE company?</summary>
      <p>
        Full foreign ownership is available for many UAE business
        activities and structures, subject to applicable laws,
        strategic-sector restrictions and licensing conditions.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Can I establish a company without renting an office?</summary>
      <p>
        Some jurisdictions offer flexi-desk or other facility
        arrangements, while other activities or authorities may
        require a physical office. Requirements must be checked
        for the selected licence.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How many visas can a Free Zone company obtain?</summary>
      <p>
        Visa eligibility depends on the jurisdiction, licence
        package, facility and applicable immigration requirements.
        Visa allocation should be confirmed before purchase.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Can I open a corporate bank account after company formation?</summary>
      <p>
        A company may apply for a corporate bank account, subject
        to the bank's independent compliance checks, documentation
        and eligibility assessment. Account approval is not guaranteed.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Will my company need VAT and Corporate Tax registration?</summary>
      <p>
        Registration and filing obligations depend on the company's
        activities, taxable supplies, income and applicable UAE
        tax rules. Obtain advice based on your actual circumstances.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How much does company formation cost in the UAE?</summary>
      <p>
        Costs vary according to jurisdiction, activity, licence
        type, facility, visa requirements and additional services.
        Request an itemised quotation before proceeding.
      </p>
    </details>

  </div>
</section>

